{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>This is that which is for the Levites.</b> Age disqualifies them, and no other thing disqualifies a Levite, for a blemish does not disqualify them. <b>For the Levites</b> — and not for the priests, for age does not disqualify priests. And this passage was said only in the wilderness, as we have learned: the Sages taught — a Levite from thirty years old until fifty is fit for service, and age disqualifies him. In what case? In the Tent of Meeting in the wilderness, when they were not settled, and the service was on the shoulder; therefore they would not carry the Ark except men of strength. But in Shiloh and in the Eternal House, where they were settled and established, they are disqualified only by voice. Rabbi Yossi said: what is the verse? ״ויהי כאחד למחצצרים ומשוררים להשמיע קול אחד״ — כאחד, even elders, במשמע קול אחד, for they need to tune their voice so that it appears as one voice. Thus it is taught, and thus Rashi explained in chapter HaKol Shochatim." "<b>From twenty-five years old.</b> And further on, in the section of BeMidbar, it says ״from thirty years old and upward.״ Rather, according to the plain sense, this passage was said for all the Levites: from twenty-five years old they all come to perform light tasks, such as standing guard so that no outsider enters the Tabernacle, and to sing, until they reach thirty. From that point on they are in their strength, and the sons of Kehat carry on the shoulder, and the sons of Gershon and Merari engage in loading and unloading the wagons and in taking down and setting up the Tabernacle."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :register {:flags {0 ["the Eternal"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:06.218578780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}